import json
R=[
("fulvia-and-mark-antony-or-fulvia-s-revenge",6,1,"Fulvia, the fierce wife of Mark Antony, takes revenge on the dead Cicero, the great speaker who had attacked her husband, in this gruesome scene from the civil wars after Caesar's death. The Spanish painter Francisco Maura y Montaner made it in 1888."),
("the-meeting-of-antony-and-cleopatra",6,0,"In 41 BC Cleopatra of Egypt arrives to meet the Roman general Mark Antony and wins him over with a spectacular show. Alma-Tadema paints her waiting under a golden canopy on her barge as Antony approaches, a meeting that changed Rome's history."),
("virgil-reading-the-aeneid-to-augustus-and-octavia",6,0,"The poet Virgil reads from his epic poem the Aeneid to the emperor Augustus and his sister Octavia, who faints at the lines about her dead son Marcellus. Angelica Kauffmann painted this famous story in 1788."),
("the-battle-of-actium",3,0,"Dozens of oared warships crash together at Actium in 31 BC, the sea battle where Octavian's fleet beat Mark Antony and Cleopatra. After it Octavian became Augustus, the first Roman emperor. Laureys a Castro painted it in 1672."),
("cleopatra-disembarking-at-tarsus",2,0,"Claude Lorrain turns the arrival of Cleopatra at Tarsus into a glowing harbor scene, where the Egyptian queen steps ashore to meet Mark Antony in the golden light of sunrise. Painted in 1642, it is more about light on water than about the story."),
("the-century-of-augustus",6,0,"Jean-Léon Gérôme shows peoples from across the Roman Empire bowing before Augustus in Rome, at the moment of peace in which, according to Christian tradition, Jesus was born. He painted it in 1855 and it shows how huge the empire had become."),
("cleopatra-s-feast",6,0,"Cleopatra bets Mark Antony that she can spend a fortune on one dinner, then drops a priceless pearl in her wine and drinks it. Jacob Jordaens shows the crowded feast in his lively Flemish style in 1653."),
("a-roman-emperor-ad-41",6,0,"After the emperor Caligula was killed in AD 41, soldiers found his uncle Claudius hiding behind a curtain and made him emperor. Lawrence Alma-Tadema, who loved Roman history, painted the moment in 1871."),
("the-triumph-of-titus",6,0,"Titus's soldiers parade through Rome in AD 71 with treasure from the conquest of Jerusalem. Lawrence Alma-Tadema painted the great procession passing on a staircase of the city in 1885."),
("the-last-words-of-marcus-aurelius",6,0,"The Roman emperor and philosopher Marcus Aurelius, dying, presents his young son Commodus to his friends and asks them to guide him, though Commodus turned out to be a bad emperor. Eugène Delacroix painted this sad scene in 1844."),
("ave-caesar-morituri-te-salutant",6,0,"Gladiators salute the emperor with the words 'we who are about to die salute you' before a fight in the Roman arena. Jean-Léon Gérôme painted this in 1859 and helped create how everyone imagines the Colosseum."),
("interior-of-the-colosseum-rome",2,0,"Thomas Cole paints the half-ruined Colosseum glowing in the Roman sun in 1832, the great arena of the emperors now open to the sky. Cole, a founder of American landscape painting, saw it on his trip to Italy and later painted a series about the rise and fall of empires."),
("the-destruction-of-pompeii-and-herculaneum",6,0,"John Martin's glowing sky and lightning show the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in AD 79 that buried Pompeii and Herculaneum. Painted in 1822, it turns the ancient disaster into a Romantic spectacle."),
("self-portrait-with-the-colosseum",1,0,"The Dutch painter Maarten van Heemskerck shows himself in front of the Colosseum in 1553, when the great arena was already a crumbling ruin. It is one of the first pictures to treat Roman ruins as something precious."),
("the-fire-of-rome",6,0,"Hubert Robert paints the Great Fire of Rome in AD 64 with a river-bridge silhouetted against the flames. According to Roman writers, Nero blamed the Christians, though many people thought he started it himself."),
("the-remorse-of-the-emperor-nero-after-the-murder-of-his",6,0,"The emperor Nero, who has just had his own mother Agrippina killed, lies on a couch filled with guilt while his attendants look away. John William Waterhouse painted this dark moment in 1878."),
("forum-romanum-for-mr-soane-s-museum",2,0,"J. M. W. Turner paints the ruins of the Roman Forum in 1826, a place where emperors and senators once walked, now crumbling in a golden haze. It was made for the collector Sir John Soane."),
("the-destruction-of-the-temple-at-jerusalem",6,1,"In AD 70 the Roman army under the future emperor Titus destroyed the Temple in Jerusalem at the end of a Jewish revolt. Nicolas Poussin painted this violent scene in 1638."),
("genseric-sacking-rome",6,1,"In 455 AD the Vandal king Genseric captured Rome and looted it for two weeks, one of the blows that weakened the Western Empire. The Russian painter Karl Bryullov painted this chaos in 1836, soon after his famous Last Day of Pompeii."),
("the-sack-of-rome-by-the-visigoths-on-24-august-410",6,0,"In 410 the Visigoths under Alaric broke into Rome, the first time in about 800 years that an enemy had taken the city. Joseph-Noël Sylvestre's big painting of 1890 shows the invaders pulling down the statues of the old gods."),
("attila-and-his-hordes-overrun-italy-and-the-arts",6,0,"Attila the Hun, whose army terrified Rome in the 450s, rides over Italy, trampling art and learning under his horses' hooves. Eugène Delacroix painted this as part of a huge ceiling decoration in Paris in the 1840s."),
("the-meeting-of-leo-the-great-and-attila",6,0,"In 452 Pope Leo I met Attila the Hun and, according to the story, persuaded him to turn his army back from Rome. Raphael painted the legend in the Vatican in 1514, with the apostles Peter and Paul appearing in the sky."),
("the-invasion-of-the-barbarians",6,0,"Ulpiano Checa, who loved painting wild horses and chariots, shows hordes of mounted warriors charging across a snowy plain. The picture imagines the peoples who pushed into the Roman Empire at the end of antiquity."),
("the-feast-of-attila",6,0,"Attila the Hun feasts with his warriors and advisors in a great hall. The Hungarian painter Mór Than painted this in 1870, when many Hungarians looked at Attila as a figure from their own early history."),
("the-triumphant-entry-of-constantine-into-rome",6,0,"The emperor Constantine rides into Rome in 312 AD after beating his rival at the Milvian Bridge, an event that opened the way for Christianity to become the empire's main religion. Peter Paul Rubens designed the scene in 1621 as part of a tapestry series."),
("the-battle-of-the-milvian-bridge",6,1,"Constantine's army defeats his rival Maxentius at the Milvian Bridge in 312 AD, a victory he said was helped by a vision of a cross. Giulio Romano painted this big battle in the Vatican around 1520."),
("the-favorites-of-the-emperor-honorius",6,0,"The weak emperor Honorius was told that Rome had fallen and said it couldn't be, he had just fed her. He meant his pet chicken, which he had named Roma. John William Waterhouse shows the emperor with his birds in 1883."),
("alaric-in-athens",6,1,"The Visigoth king Alaric enters Athens in 396 AD, and the city's people stand before him in fear. Ludwig Thiersch painted this scene of the later fall of the classical world in 1879."),
("constantius-appoints-constantine-as-his-successor",6,0,"Constantius, a Roman emperor, names his son Constantine as his successor in 306 AD, and Constantine goes on to become the first Christian emperor. Peter Paul Rubens painted this scene in 1622 for a series about Constantine's life."),
("theodosius-and-saint-ambrose",7,0,"In 390 Bishop Ambrose of Milan stands in the church doorway and refuses to let the Emperor Theodosius enter until he repents for a terrible massacre. The story shows the Church becoming powerful enough to stand up to emperors. Rubens painted it in 1617 and Van Dyck made this version soon after."),
("the-battle-of-poitiers-732",6,0,"In 732 the Frankish leader Charles Martel stopped a Muslim army from advancing farther into France at the Battle of Tours and Poitiers, and his grandson was Charlemagne. Charles de Steuben painted this clash in 1837."),
("the-battle-of-tolbiac-496",6,1,"Clovis, king of the Franks, vows to become a Christian if he wins at Tolbiac against the Alemanni, and then he does. Ary Scheffer painted this founding moment of France in 1836."),
("the-death-of-roland",6,0,"The hero Roland, one of Charlemagne's knights, dies after fighting at Roncesvalles in 778, in the legend that became the Song of Roland. Jean Fouquet painted it in a French royal manuscript around 1455."),
("muslim-troops-leaving-narbonne-to-pepin-the-short-759",6,0,"Pepin the Short, Charlemagne's father, finally takes the city of Narbonne in 759, driving out the Muslim garrison. This black-and-white illustration by Émile Bayard was made in 1880 for a history of France."),
("the-baptism-of-clovis",7,0,"Clovis, the king of the Franks, is baptized by a bishop around the year 496, which made France a Christian kingdom. The painter, known only as the Master of Saint Giles, made this panel around 1500."),
("the-coronation-of-charlemagne",6,0,"On Christmas Day in 800, Pope Leo III crowns Charlemagne emperor in Rome, the first emperor in the West in over 300 years. Raphael painted this ceremony in the Vatican around 1516, centuries later."),
("the-coronation-of-charlemagne-grandes-chroniques-de-fra",6,0,"This glowing little picture of Charlemagne's crowning comes from the Grandes Chroniques de France, the French royal history. Jean Fouquet, the court painter, made it around 1458."),
("the-building-of-the-chapel-at-aachen-grandes-chroniques",6,0,"Workers build the great chapel at Aachen, Charlemagne's capital, using ladders and stone blocks. The scene is from the Grandes Chroniques de France, illustrated by Jean Fouquet around 1458."),
("the-fall-of-king-olav-at-the-battle-of-stiklestad",6,1,"King Olav II falls at the Battle of Stiklestad in 1030. He was later made Saint Olaf, the patron saint of Norway. Peter Nicolai Arbo painted it in the 1850s."),
("the-battle-of-stamford-bridge",6,1,"In 1066 King Harald Hardrada of Norway, the last great Viking king, is killed in a battle against the English at Stamford Bridge. Peter Nicolai Arbo painted this clash in 1870, only days before the Norman invasion."),
("harald-fairhair-in-the-battle-of-hafrsfjord",6,0,"Harald Fairhair wins the sea battle of Hafrsfjord around the year 872, a victory the sagas say united Norway under one king. The Norwegian-American painter Ole Peter Hansen Balling painted it in 1870."),
("the-battle-of-svolder",3,0,"At the sea battle of Svolder in the year 1000, King Olav Tryggvason's famous ship the Long Serpent was surrounded by enemy ships. According to the sagas he leapt overboard rather than be captured. Otto Sinding painted it in 1883."),
("olav-tryggvason-s-arrival-in-norway",6,0,"Olav Tryggvason sails back to Norway in 995 to take the throne, and the sagas say he then pushed his people to become Christian. Peter Nicolai Arbo made this black-and-white scene in 1860."),
("the-captured-king-gryting-is-brought-before-king-harald",6,0,"The conquered king Gryting is brought before Harald Fairhair in a scene from the Viking sagas. Erik Werenskiold drew it in 1899 for an illustrated edition of Snorri Sturluson's Heimskringla, the saga of the Norwegian kings."),
("guests-from-overseas",6,0,"Viking-age traders, called Varangians, sail a dragon-headed ship into a Slavic harbor in this glowing scene. The Russian painter Nicholas Roerich, who loved ancient history, painted it in 1901."),
]
